# Auth Broker GitHub Identity Boundary

The `auth-broker-tee` repository is privacy-sensitive. Do not associate a
personal GitHub account with repository write operations or release decisions.

Required identity boundary:

- `FemLed-CI`: creates all code commits, including commits added to pull
  request branches, pushes branches, opens pull requests, and merges after
  required status checks pass.

When working in this repository:

- Do not create code commits using a personal/user GitHub identity, including
  commits made while opening, updating, or fixing pull requests.
- Do not push branches using a personal/user GitHub token.
- Do not open, close, merge, or otherwise manage pull requests using a
  personal/user GitHub identity.
- Do not bypass branch protection, required signatures, or
  required status checks.
- Any commit, push, branch creation, pull request creation, merge, or
  release/deploy action must be performed through `FemLed-CI`.
- Do not introduce a machine-user PR approval shim. The TEE First Principles
  status check is the review gate; GitHub PR approvals are not the trust root.

If the active git/GitHub identity is not clearly the correct app identity for
the operation, stop before any write operation and ask the user to switch
credentials or provide the approved CI mechanism.

## Minting a FemLed-CI GitHub App Token

Use a short-lived GitHub App installation token from GCP Secret Manager. Do not
use `gh auth login`, the keychain token, or a personal PAT for write operations.

```bash
APP_ID=$(gcloud secrets versions access latest \
  --project="prod-femled-couple-router" \
  --secret="femled-ci-github-app-id")

PRIVATE_KEY=$(gcloud secrets versions access latest \
  --project="prod-femled-couple-router" \
  --secret="femled-ci-github-app-private-key")

GH_TOKEN=$(APP_ID="$APP_ID" PRIVATE_KEY="$PRIVATE_KEY" node --input-type=module <<'NODE'
import crypto from 'node:crypto';

const owner = 'FemLed';
const repo = 'auth-broker-tee';

function b64url(value) {
  return Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(value)).toString('base64url');
}

function appJwt() {
  const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);
  const header = b64url({ alg: 'RS256', typ: 'JWT' });
  const payload = b64url({ iat: now - 60, exp: now + 540, iss: process.env.APP_ID });
  const unsigned = `${header}.${payload}`;
  const key = process.env.PRIVATE_KEY.replace(/\\n/g, '\n');
  const sig = crypto.sign('RSA-SHA256', Buffer.from(unsigned), key).toString('base64url');
  return `${unsigned}.${sig}`;
}

async function api(path, { method = 'GET', token, body } = {}) {
  const response = await fetch(`https://api.github.com${path}`, {
    method,
    headers: {
      Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
      Accept: 'application/vnd.github+json',
      'X-GitHub-Api-Version': '2022-11-28',
      'User-Agent': 'FemLed-CI-token-mint',
      ...(body ? { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } : {}),
    },
    body: body ? JSON.stringify(body) : undefined,
  });
  const text = await response.text();
  const json = text ? JSON.parse(text) : null;
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`${method} ${path} failed ${response.status}: ${text}`);
  return json;
}

const jwt = appJwt();
const installation = await api(`/repos/${owner}/${repo}/installation`, { token: jwt });
const token = await api(`/app/installations/${installation.id}/access_tokens`, {
  method: 'POST',
  token: jwt,
});

process.stdout.write(token.token);
NODE
)

export GH_TOKEN
gh api user --jq .login
```

After use, run `unset GH_TOKEN APP_ID PRIVATE_KEY`. Never print or commit the
token or private key. Request narrower installation permissions in the Node
body when a task only needs a subset of the app's granted permissions.
